# ute_ue

[![Documentation](https://docs.taf.ute.nsn-rdnet.net/projects/ute_ue/badge/)][1]
[![Requirements](https://taf.wrgitlab-pages.int.net.nokia.com/miscellaneous/static-badges/requirements.svg)](requirements/base.txt)
[![build status](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/abstract_library/ute_ue/badges/main/pipeline.svg)][2]
[![coverage report](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/abstract_library/ute_ue/badges/main/coverage.svg)][2]
[![latest release](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/abstract_library/ute_ue/-/badges/release.svg)][3]

This version of ute_ue library supports following functionality:
- Require Ue keyword to take ue into use from available ues
- Attach and Detach for UE
- Data Transfer handling (start, stop and verify throughput)
- Voice Call (start, stop, await finish)

Ue types that are currently supported:
- WTS/IPHY simulated UEs
    WTS has to be running (in ACTIVE state) with simulated UEs before the ute_ue library can be used.
- Android UEs with Voice Calls

PLEASE DO NOT COMMIT ANYTHING TO SVN AS RELEASES FROM GIT DEVELOPMENT REPOSITORY WILL OVERWRITE YOUR CHANGES

## Supported Python versions

Library should work properly with Python versions specified within
`python_requires` option in [setup.py](setup.py).

## Installation

Generic library installation process is described in [TAF user guide][4].

## UE configuration

Ue configuration may be given in following ways:
1. ABSTRACT_LIB_CONFIG robot variable. It has to be introduced at the Test Suite level.
   It can contain either path to configuration file or direct configuration as a dictionary.
2. ABSTRACT_LIB_CONFIG environment variable. It can only contain path to configuration file.
Robot variable takes precedence over environment variable.

3. UTE_UE_CONFIG robot variable.
4. UTE_UE_CONFIG environment variable.
(same notes as for ABSTRACT_LIB_CONFIG)

ute_ue itself requires configuration with following structure:
UE_POOLS:
    UeTypeAUePool:
        <parameters specific for UeTypeAUePool>

    UeTypeBUePool:
        <parameters specific for UeTypeAUePool>

as you can see ute_ue may work on testlines with mixed UE-pools,
for example one UE-pool handles simulated UEs and second handles real-UEs with RFpath.

Configuration file examples: see ute_ue/example/config folder

Each implementation of UE (ute_ue_plugin_XXX) has freedom how configuration is defined.
It may be config-file, database stored config or autodetected config.
For details of such configuration please do read documentation of specific plugin.

